## 10. Parent and Student class-change requests

### 10.1 Feature identity

Names:

- French: `Demande de changement de classe`
- Arabic: `طلب تغيير القسم`
- English: `Class Change Request`

This is a structured administrative request, not a normal chat message, Parent Note or Attendance justification.

### 10.2 Student permissions

An approved Student can submit a request only for their own server-verified student identity and active membership.

No ability to select another student.

### 10.3 Parent permissions

An approved Parent may select only their verified linked children.

One Parent may request a transfer for one child without affecting siblings.

The relationship must be checked again by the backend at submission and read time.

### 10.4 Request form

Fields:

| Field | Behavior |
|---|---|
| Student | Own student or verified linked child |
| Current class | Server-derived, read-only |
| Academic year | Server-derived |
| Desired class | Authorized same-year eligible choices |
| Reason category | Structured selection |
| Explanation | Required, length-bounded |
| Submission date | Server-generated |
| Request reference | Server-generated |

Suggested reason categories:

- Pedagogical/academic.
- Social integration.
- Wellbeing.
- Other.

Sensitive explanations must not be exposed to classmates, unrelated Teachers or the public.

A requester may indicate no specific desired class and ask the administration to propose one. This needs an explicit accepted product rule before enabling.

### 10.5 Request states

Proposed workflow:

`SUBMITTED → UNDER_REVIEW → APPROVED / REJECTED`

Also support `CANCELLED` when the requester is eligible to withdraw an undecided request.

If approval of the request and actual transfer require separate administrative execution, distinguish:

- Decision approved.
- Transfer pending.
- Transfer completed.
- Transfer failed/conflicted.

Do not label a student as transferred merely because a reviewer clicked Approve.

### 10.6 Duplicate and stale requests

The backend must enforce an explicit duplicate-request policy.

Recommended initial behavior:

- Allow at most one unresolved class-change request per student and effective current membership.
- A terminal request remains in history.
- A new request after a completed decision can be submitted subject to school policy.
- If the student has moved since submission, the request becomes stale and cannot transfer the old membership blindly.

This recommendation requires acceptance before enforcement.

