## 16. Required acceptance tests

### Class creation

- Approved Owner creates a valid class.
- Approved Manager/Administrative Personnel/Teacher creates a class according to their effective individual permission.
- Owner denial blocks that person even when their role normally permits creation.
- Removing the denial restores creation without changing unrelated permissions.
- Unapproved accounts and unauthorized roles are rejected by the server.
- Empty classes are valid.
- Additional classes can be created after registration starts.
- Duplicate class names within a year/level are rejected.
- Arbitrary unsupported academic years are rejected.

### Enrollment and placement

- Student identity is created once.
- Existing student can be placed without duplication.
- Unrelated Parent cannot link to the child.
- Ineligible academic year/class placement is rejected.
- Enrollment and class placement remain distinct.
- Class roster refresh shows committed server data.

### Teacher assignment

- Approved authorized staff can assign Teachers.
- A Teacher denied creation still retains their own assigned-class capabilities.
- Class creation alone does not grant Teacher-assignment rights.
- Assignment revocation removes current class authority.
- Independent Attendance register ownership remains intact.

### Transfer

- Same-year authorized transfer succeeds once.
- Duplicate or simultaneous transfers cannot create two active memberships.
- Stale source membership fails.
- Old class history remains accessible to authorized historical readers.
- New current roster reflects the student.
- Prior Attendance is not rewritten.
- Unauthorized actors cannot transfer students.
- Effective-date rules follow the approved contract.

### Class-change requests

- Parent can request for verified linked child.
- Parent cannot request for another family's child.
- Student can request only for self.
- Pending request appears in authorized Manager and Office queues.
- Reviewer without current approval permission cannot decide.
- Approving a request leads to exactly one valid transfer.
- Rejecting a request leaves membership unchanged.
- Conflicting decisions cannot both succeed.
- Requester can read only authorized history.
- Sensitive reasons do not appear in public or unrelated notifications.
- Read access is denied after account or relevant relationship revocation.

### End-to-end

Run real authenticated allow/deny cases against an isolated Supabase database with representative synthetic records, not only mocked API calls.

Confirm relevant browser/mobile behavior and Arabic/French/English presentation.

Re-run existing Attendance, Teacher, Calendar, Directory, Parent Notes, governance and other protected regression suites.

